[#:seon.task{:name "recording-a-def-of-a-large-map-copies-it"
             :plan "Recording a `def` of a large map (one holding MCP replies) cost 800 ms and 896 MB on default (2026-10-17, MCP `eval_clj` on an agent branch), including 174 MB in the writer for one transaction. The stored form is decided once, by `seon.blob/inline-or-stage` (`:seon.config.eval.result/blob-threshold` UTF-8 bytes inline, a konserve blob above it), so a value over the threshold must be recorded as a blob digest and size on the evaluation's fact, never copied into the transaction. Find which recording step copies the big value into datoms or prints it before the decision (the producer of the stored form for a `def`'s value and its declaration facts; `seon.turn.batch`, `seon.turn/record-evaluated-tx` and the printed-value path are the candidates), and make that step call `seon.blob/inline-or-stage` once and pass the reference down. Done when recording a `def` of a map of about 1 MB printed costs under 50 MB and 100 ms on a quiet JVM and the transaction holds a blob reference, asserted through `seon.profile/measure` in the new deftest `seon.blob-test/recording-a-def-of-a-large-map-stages-it-as-a-blob` (written by a later lane; red on HEAD: 800 ms / 896 MB). Read `seon.blob/inline-or-stage` and `seon.profile/measure`."
             :proofs #{seon.blob-test/recording-a-def-of-a-large-map-stages-it-as-a-blob}}
